# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written before `git init`, on purpose. Several of the exclusions below are not tidiness:
# they are personal data, third-party material without a redistribution licence, and a private
# meeting transcript. Once any of that lands in a commit, removing it later does not remove it
# from the history.
#
# Verify before the first commit:
#   git add -A --dry-run | less          # read the whole list
#   git check-ignore -v administrativo abstract 00_data 01_scripts/DM_JOSE.R
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- must never be published ------------------------------------------------------------
# Registration forms and an invoice, carrying personal and financial details of two people.
administrativo/
# Submission drafts, with a co-author's address in the metadata.
abstract/
# The project's internal working documents. Not secret, but not for this audience either: they are
# Obsidian notes written for the next working session, so they carry [[wikilinks]] that GitHub
# renders as literal text, HPC account names and paths, raw meeting notes containing candid
# judgements about third parties, and a photograph of a personal notebook. What a reader of this
# repository needs is in README.md, 00_data/README.md and THIRD_PARTY.md, written for them.
info/
handoffs/
_log.md

# Smoke-test output from a --maxst run. No script reads it.
chill_maxst40.csv

# Third-party code without a licence to redistribute. DM_JOSE.R is the Dynamic Model under the
# Fishman et al. (1987) parametrisation, written by J.A. Egea; 00_data/README.md explains how to
# obtain it and 00_paths.R fails with instructions when it is absent.
01_scripts/DM_JOSE.R
CP_Tdiarias.zip

# Station coordinates compiled by the regional agrometeorological services, received through a
# third party. No terms of transfer, so neither they nor anything that reproduces them.
00_data/*.xlsx
02_outputs/matching_regional_to_aemet.*
02_outputs/regional_stations_elevation.csv
02_outputs/matching_map.png

# --- credentials --------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.Renviron

# --- external data (gigabytes, third-party licences; see 00_data/README.md) ----------------
00_data/*
!00_data/README.md
!00_data/stations_obs.txt

# --- generated output ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything under 02_outputs/ is regenerable from the scripts, and the chill tables run to 153 MB.
# Only the small summary tables that back a figure or a claim are versioned, listed one by one so
# that a new output has to be added deliberately rather than swept in.
02_outputs/*
!02_outputs/talk_numbers_cropland.csv
!02_outputs/cropland_threshold_sweep.csv
!02_outputs/cropland_threshold_check.csv
!02_outputs/cropland_threshold_meta.csv
!02_outputs/cieza_seasons.csv
!02_outputs/cieza_parametrisation_gap.csv
!02_outputs/cieza_check_summary.csv
!02_outputs/api_vs_archive_summary.csv
!02_outputs/api_vs_archive_threshold_sweep.csv
!02_outputs/api_vs_archive_by_station.csv
!02_outputs/observed_annual_series.csv
!02_outputs/observed_long_record_summary.csv
!02_outputs/observed_panel_sensitivity.csv
!02_outputs/observed_swc_by_window.csv
!02_outputs/observed_spliced_swc.csv
!02_outputs/observed_spliced_summary.csv
!02_outputs/aemet_station_inventory_public.csv

# The deck: 26 MB of embedded figures, rebuilt in two minutes by scripts 29 and 30.
03_presentacion/
# ...except the one-page workflow sheet. It is 0.4 MB, it is what a new reader should see first,
# and the README links to it. Rebuilt by 44_workflow_sheet.py.
!03_presentacion/
03_presentacion/*
!03_presentacion/plinius_workflow.pdf

# --- caches and editor droppings -----------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*_cache/
*_files/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
.Ruserdata
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- the method book ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sources are versioned; the compiled book is not. It is 11 MB of generated HTML and PDF that any
# clone can rebuild in two minutes, and it would double the size of the repository for nothing.
04_metodo/_book/
04_metodo/figuras/
# Small tables that bookdown copies in because chapters link to them. They are duplicates of
# 02_outputs/ and get recreated on every render.
04_metodo/02_outputs/
# The cold-read audit: candid internal assessment of the document, same category as info/.
04_metodo/_auditoria_*.md

# R opens a default graphics device when a script plots without ggsave, and drops this here.
Rplots.pdf
**/Rplots.pdf

# --- the frozen Spanish originals -----------------------------------------------------------
# Snapshots taken on 2026-08-24, when the talk and its figures moved to English. They are exact
# twins of scripts that still exist in their migrated form, so a reader gains nothing from them
# and a maintainer would have two copies of every figure to keep in step. `legacy/README.md` and
# `legacy/build_aemet_matching.py` stay versioned because they document an abandoned line of work
# that has no successor; these do not.
01_scripts/legacy/es_figuras_2026-08-24/
01_scripts/legacy/talk_content_es_*.py
